hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2892","Narrated to us ‘Ali ibn Hujr who said: Narrated to us Isma‘il ibn Ja‘far who said: Narrated to us Ja‘far ibn Muhammad ibn ‘Ali ibn Husayn ibn ‘Ali ibn Abi Talib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir ibn ‘Abd Allah.

And narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bashshar who said: Narrated to us Yahya ibn Sa‘id who said: Narrated to us Ja‘far who said: My father narrated to me who said: We came to Jabir ibn ‘Abd Allah and he said: “The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) slaughtered sixty-three camels with his own hand. Then he gave the remaining to ‘Ali (RA) who slaughtered them.”

‘Ali ibn Hujr also said: “‘Ali slaughtered what remained.”

**CHAPTER:**"
